-Each track has **three note-effect slots** for **Note tail** (envelope release) and
-**Note echo** (note repeats with tempo divisions and velocity decay), followed by a
-**Shared** row. Audio processors run in the shared rack. Press **FX** for the track's
-rack; KNOB 2 selects its row, KNOB 1 the effect, and KNOB 4 its amount. OCT+ opens the
-selected slot, its effect picker if empty, or the shared rack; SELECT visits the racks
-and occupied slots. Note tail has its single REL control on the rack; Note echo has
-LEVEL, TIME and DECAY on its page.
+Every effect sits in one of two racks, routed as in [Araminta](https://github.com/Wulgaren/Araminta)'s EFFECTS
+list: **CHAIN** on a track, **SEND** or **MASTER** in the shared rack.
 
-The shared rack's audio choices are **Phaser, Width, Formant, Tape, Spit, Room, Reverb,
-Chorus, Drive, Crush, Flanger, Pedal phaser and Pedal chorus**, grouped into Space,
-Motion, Dirt and Colour. OCT+ on an empty shared slot opens the effect browser: KNOB 1
-selects a family, KNOB 2 an effect, and OCT+ confirms. Audio processors in older projects' track
-slots load OFF; recreate them in the shared rack and set the track's send.
+**A track's rack (FX):** three insert slots in series (CHAIN), then a **Shared** row. A slot holds any audio effect
+or a note effect (**Note tail**, an envelope release, and **Note echo**, note repeats with tempo divisions and
+velocity decay). KNOB 2 selects the row, KNOB 1 the effect, KNOB 3 its **ORDER** (1st, 2nd, 3rd: the effect moves,
+with all its controls, and the row follows) and KNOB 4 its MIX. The Shared row's KNOB 4 is the track's SEND. OCT+
+opens the selected slot, its effect picker if empty, or the shared rack; SELECT visits the racks and occupied slots.
+Note tail has its single REL control on the rack; Note echo has LEVEL, TIME and DECAY on its page.
+
+**The shared rack (SHARED):** three slots and RETURN. KNOB 3 on a slot is its **USE**: **SEND** (fed by the tracks'
+SEND, mixed back at RETURN) or **MASTER** (the whole mix runs through it, after the returns and before the punch FX
+and MASTER volume; KNOB 4 its MIX, dry to wet). KNOB 3 on RETURN is **ROUTE**: in CHAIN each track's SEND feeds the
+SEND slots in series; in SPLIT each SEND slot has its own track send. A MASTER slot shows MASTER on its row, and a
+track's Shared row lists only the slots its SEND reaches.
+
+The audio choices are **Room, Reverb, Delay, Width, Phaser, Chorus, Flanger, Pedal phaser, Pedal chorus, Drive,
+Crush, Formant, Tape and Spit**, grouped into Space, Motion, Dirt and Colour. OCT+ on an empty slot opens the effect
+browser: KNOB 1 selects a family, KNOB 2 an effect, and OCT+ confirms. **Reverb** and **Delay** run once each (their
+tanks take 19 KiB and 32 KiB): choosing one in any slot turns it off where it was.
+
+**Delay** is a tempo-synced mono delay at 22.05 kHz with a 0.74 s tank: TIME (1/32, 1/16T, 1/16, 1/8T, 1/16D, 1/8,
+1/4T, 1/8D, 1/4, 1/2T, 1/4D, 1/2 of the beat; a time longer than the tank is halved until it fits), FDBK (repeats)
+and TONE (the input's cuts), each repeat a little darker. A time change glides like tape.
 
