         <p>Hold <kbd>FX</kbd> and press a key to apply one of SLOOP’s 27 audio effects to the whole stereo master, including shared returns and USB stereo capture. Release the effect key for dry audio. Double-tap FX to lock the layer and tap again to close. KNOB 1 browses the key reference. Keys held before FX keep playing; effect keys produce no notes or MIDI.</p>
         <p>The effects include loops, reverse, tape stop, half speed, filter sweeps, phone, crush, alias, gate, echo, wobble, band kills, rewind, octave up, flanger, auto-pan, freeze, mono and fade. FREEZE uses SLOOP Reverb to hold 186 ms of captured master audio. The optional punch history uses 32 KiB while the layer is in use (372 ms of mono history; replay spans up to 348 ms); hold FX briefly before reverse/rewind. If memory is unavailable the header shows FX MEMORY; close FX, reduce effect memory use and reopen to retry.</p>
         <h3>Shared return</h3>
-        <p>The Shared row feeds one shared three-slot return after this track’s level and pan. In the <strong>SHARED</strong> rack, <kbd>KNOB 2</kbd> selects slots A–C or RETURN, <kbd>KNOB 1</kbd> chooses a slot’s effect, <kbd>KNOB 3</kbd> sets <strong>ROUTE</strong>, and <kbd>KNOB 4</kbd> sets the selected amount. <kbd>OCT+</kbd> opens a slot. Hold <kbd>OCT+</kbd>, or tap it on RETURN, for Routing and Clear shared FX (asks first).</p>
+        <p>The Shared row feeds the shared rack after this track’s level and pan. In the <strong>SHARED</strong> rack, <kbd>KNOB 2</kbd> selects slots A–C or RETURN and <kbd>KNOB 1</kbd> chooses a slot’s effect. <kbd>KNOB 3</kbd> on a slot sets its <strong>USE</strong>: <strong>SEND</strong> (fed by the tracks’ SEND, mixed back at RETURN) or <strong>MASTER</strong> (the whole mix runs through it, after the returns and before the punch effects and MASTER volume; <kbd>KNOB 4</kbd> its MIX, dry to wet). A MASTER slot shows MASTER on its row, and a track’s Shared row lists only the slots its SEND reaches. <kbd>KNOB 3</kbd> on RETURN sets <strong>ROUTE</strong>:</p>
         <ul>
           <li><strong>CHAIN</strong> (default) — raise the selected track’s SEND on FX’s Shared row. Slots A–C run in series. On SHARED, <kbd>KNOB 4</kbd> sets each slot’s MIX, initially fully wet, or the overall RETURN.</li>
           <li><strong>SPLIT</strong> — each shared slot has its own send. On SHARED, <kbd>KNOB 4</kbd> sets this track’s SEND to the selected slot, or RETURN on the last row. Each slot’s return joins the dry output. SEND 2 and SEND 3 are remembered when you go back to CHAIN. Shared slot pages still edit their MIX.</li>
         </ul>
-        <p>Only one shared REVERB can be active: choosing it in another shared slot moves it there; imported duplicate REVERB slots keep the first. Historical per-track audio processors load OFF and are not moved automatically. Recreate those processors in SHARED and set the track sends. NOTE TAIL and NOTE ECHO remain per-track. Existing shared settings keep their supported compatibility paths; older firmware may not reproduce the new routing.</p>
+        <p>Older projects’ per-track audio effects load again into their track slots. A project that uses MASTER or DELAY does not load on earlier firmware.</p>
